<figure class="lms-figure" aria-labelledby="fig-break">
  <figcaption id="fig-break" class="lms-figure-caption">First moves when the terminal misbehaves</figcaption>
  <ul class="lms-fixes">
    <li class="lms-fix"><span class="lms-fix-symptom">“Terminal not connected”</span><span class="lms-fix-do">Check its Wi-Fi or SIM signal and power. Restart the P18. Try again from Rupert. Still down → take cash or use the backup terminal, then call.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-fix"><span class="lms-fix-symptom">Declined</span><span class="lms-fix-do">Say “the bank declined it” and ask for another card. Never retry the same card over and over, never ask for the number to key it in.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-fix"><span class="lms-fix-symptom">Tap worked, Rupert says “waiting”</span><span class="lms-fix-do">Do not charge again. Use <strong>Recheck</strong> on the sale; Rupert asks the terminal what happened. One tap, one charge.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-fix"><span class="lms-fix-symptom">Batch did not close</span><span class="lms-fix-do">Close it from checkout setup (or the terminal menu) before leaving. Tips cannot be adjusted once it does, and nothing is deposited until it does.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-fix"><span class="lms-fix-symptom">Totals do not match</span><span class="lms-fix-do">Terminal batch report vs Rupert's register summary. Do not “fix” by re-ringing. Note the difference and hand it to the owner.</span></li>
  </ul>
</figure>
